    <string name="a11y_label">Sidepeek side panel</string>
    <string name="a11y_summary">Shows the message side panel without a persistent notification</string>
    <string name="a11y_description">This accessibility service is only used to:\n1. Show the Peek bar (a small handle at the screen edge) and the side panel, without a persistent notification and without the system’s “displaying over other apps” notice;\n2. Tell whether you are on the home screen, for “Show only on home screen”;\n3. Tell whether the keyboard is open, to hide the Peek bar for a while;\n4. Receive the Back key while the side panel is open, to close it;\n5. Clear the LINE notifications Sidepeek organized when you open LINE.\n\nBy default the service only checks which app’s window is in front, whether a keyboard window is open, and key presses. It never reads, stores or sends any text or content on the screen, and it never taps or acts for you. Only if you separately turn on “Advanced clearing” in the app (off by default; you are asked to agree when turning it on) does it read the chat name at the top of LINE’s screen, compared on the phone only, never stored or uploaded.</string>

